-- title:
--   Twisted Γ-orbits coincide with Γ'-orbits on Deligne data
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a commutative ring $\mathcal O$, an element $\pi \in \mathcal O$, a field $K_0$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: $Onr$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^{r}$ lies in it for all $x$. Let $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) be a homomorphism, $G$ a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism, and $\Gamma \le G$ a subgroup containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ and $v\!\det(\sigma z) = 2$; let $\Gamma' \le G$ be a subgroup whose elements are exactly the $x \in \Gamma$ with $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ even. Let $B$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, $\psi : Onr \to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and $P, P'$ Deligne data over $B$, that is, families assigning to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ with invertible quotient, compatible with lattice inclusions, invariant under scalar homotheties, and satisfying the nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $B$. The assertion is the equivalence of: (i) there is $\gamma \in \Gamma$ with $\psi = \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v\det(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $P'$ the pull-back of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, i.e. for every full lattice $M$ the line of $P'$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $P$ at $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed action isomorphism; and (ii) there is $\gamma' \in \Gamma'$ with $P'$ the pull-back of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma')^{-1}$, no condition on $\psi$ being imposed.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic bookkeeping step in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description of the $p$-adic upper half plane with unramified coefficients: at a fixed coefficient map $\psi$, the Frobenius-twisted orbit relation of $\Gamma$ on pairs $(\psi, P)$ reduces to the untwisted orbit relation of the even-determinant-valuation subgroup $\Gamma'$ on Deligne data, the discrepancy being absorbed by the central element $z$, whose scalar image acts trivially on Deligne data. It is used in the analysis of the fibres of the descended quotient map.
